                                                "sense_id": "ff4f1da2-1cae-30ec-94c1-e865efd18eb3",
                                                "text": "Take the rule about pronouns and possessives that Mr. Keegan cited in his challenge to the testing service."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "403c9f31-425d-4f20-9b4b-78c7ea6ee88c",
                                                "sense_id": "ff4f1da2-1cae-30ec-94c1-e865efd18eb3",
                                                "text": "The New York Times, The Washington Post and The Wall Street Journal all do the opposite, opting for ’s to mark a singular possessive and a simple apostrophe for plural possessive (Harrises’ and Walzes’)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
